---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const normalizeDonationsResult = await normalizeDonations(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const interpretNeedsResult = await interpretNeeds(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, normalizeDonationsResult.accepted);
const constructBundlesResult = await constructBundles(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, interpretNeedsResult.accepted);
const applyAllocationResult = await applyAllocation(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, constructBundlesResult.accepted);
const coordinateDeliveryResult = await coordinateDelivery(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, applyAllocationResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { normalizeDonations: normalizeDonationsResult, interpretNeeds: interpretNeedsResult, constructBundles: constructBundlesResult, applyAllocation: applyAllocationResult, coordinateDelivery: coordinateDeliveryResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...normalizeDonationsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...interpretNeedsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...constructBundlesResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...applyAllocationResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...coordinateDeliveryResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...normalizeDonationsResult.checks, ...interpretNeedsResult.checks, ...constructBundlesResult.checks, ...applyAllocationResult.checks, ...coordinateDeliveryResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A donor changes the quantity on collection day: recompute affected allocations without hiding unmet needs. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (recompute affected allocations without hiding unmet needs.) through the existing stage result for DonationOffer; preserve exact source/version and the prior DonationOffer, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — A recipient cannot store a large bundle: split delivery or propose a suitable alternative. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (split delivery or propose a suitable alternative.) through the existing stage result for DonationOffer; preserve exact source/version and the prior DonationOffer, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — A donor requests private recipient details: provide only consented information. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (provide only consented information.) through the existing stage result for DonationOffer; preserve exact source/version and the prior DonationOffer, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — A recipient declines an item: preserve dignity and reallocate without penalizing future need. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (preserve dignity and reallocate without penalizing future need.) through the existing stage result for DonationOffer; preserve exact source/version and the prior DonationOffer, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — An item has a recall or handling restriction: quarantine it under the supplied safety policy. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (quarantine it under the supplied safety policy.) through the existing stage result for DonationOffer; preserve exact source/version and the prior DonationOffer, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, normalizeDonations: normalizeDonationsResult, interpretNeeds: interpretNeedsResult, constructBundles: constructBundlesResult, applyAllocation: applyAllocationResult, coordinateDelivery: coordinateDeliveryResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
